{"authored" [{"question" "q-152762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{{z}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{{z}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}z & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{8}^{a}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{{z}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{8}^{a}{z}^{-4/3}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-3{z}^{-1/3}]}_{8}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{z}}]}_{8}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{a}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{8}}) \\\\  & =-6(0-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-152762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "The integral diverges"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{4}+2)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u={x}^{4}+2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=4{x}^{3}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{4}+2$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{4}+2)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{4}+2)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-2{u}^{-1/2}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-1/2}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{1/2}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{1/2}}] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{(5\\theta +1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=5\\theta +1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=5\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $\\theta \\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=5\\theta +1$ is as follows:\n\n| $\\theta $ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{(5\\theta +1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{5{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{(5\\theta +1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{5{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{5}{u}^{-2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350532" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-350532" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following improper integrals are divergent?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(z+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z$\n- ${\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's work out each integral.\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2{u}^{2}}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{2(-2)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2{a}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2{a}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nFor the second integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(z+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{(z+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{z+3}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{a+3}+\\frac{1}{0+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nFor the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]_{2}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡a-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\n\nIn conclusion, only integrals III is divergent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-6032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following improper integrals are divergent?\n\n- ${\\int }_{10}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-6032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's work out each integral.\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{10}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{10}^{a}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[2\\sqrt{x-1}]}_{10}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(2\\sqrt{a-1}-2\\sqrt{10-1}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(2\\sqrt{a-1}-6) \\\\  & =\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\n\nFor the second integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|a|) \\\\  & =-\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\n\nFor the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nIn conclusion, only integrals I and II are divergent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-6032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-6032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3d7c2d94962f4ae10712300270f0bbaea1efda05c305e45bc2237f1a8712d7e" "basis" 1137 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-6032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/m